1
00:00:00,867 --> 00:00:01,767
<i>Have you thought about
your request?</i>

2
00:00:01,900 --> 00:00:03,533
<i>I need to know
where I can find Berdugo.</i>

3
00:00:03,800 --> 00:00:06,267
<i>You're like someone searching
for a shadow in the dark.</i>

4
00:00:06,400 --> 00:00:08,967
<i> Shadow appears in the light.</i>

5
00:00:09,100 --> 00:00:11,333
<i>Godfather and Braganza
are now feuding</i>

6
00:00:11,467 --> 00:00:12,533
<i> because of what happened.</i>

7
00:00:12,667 --> 00:00:13,900
<i>It's not just an ordinary fight.</i>

8
00:00:14,033 --> 00:00:15,367
<i>The two of them will end up
killing each other.</i>

9
00:00:15,500 --> 00:00:16,733
<i> Let them waste each other.</i>

10
00:00:16,867 --> 00:00:18,733
<i>According to our reliable
source,</i>

11
00:00:18,867 --> 00:00:21,200
<i>the wanted drug dealer
in Bolagos is known</i>

12
00:00:21,333 --> 00:00:23,600
<i> by the name Loloy.</i>

13
00:00:24,367 --> 00:00:26,733
<i>I'm sure Loloy's face will
spread quickly in the press.</i>

14
00:00:26,867 --> 00:00:29,367
<i>We need to know who
the whistleblower is.</i>

15
00:00:29,500 --> 00:00:30,700
<i> Then let's find out who it is.</i>

16
00:00:30,833 --> 00:00:32,067
<i>- Tomas?
- Andrew...</i>

17
00:00:32,200 --> 00:00:34,000
<i>You've released
a big story today.</i>

18
00:00:34,167 --> 00:00:35,400
<i>Tell me.
Who is your source?</i>

19
00:00:35,533 --> 00:00:37,700
<i>You know I don't burn
my sources, right?</i>

20
00:00:37,833 --> 00:00:38,833
<i> He didn't even say anything.</i>

21
00:00:38,967 --> 00:00:40,500
<i>- Actually, he did.
- Golda.</i>

22
00:00:40,633 --> 00:00:41,833
<i> I'll be watching you for now.</i>

23
00:00:41,967 --> 00:00:43,867
<i>Am I really the one you're going
to watch over?</i>

24
00:00:44,000 --> 00:00:45,100
<i> Or your boyfriend?</i>

25
00:00:45,233 --> 00:00:46,133
<i> You're so dramatic!</i>

26
00:00:46,267 --> 00:00:47,967
<i> Golda isn't in police custody.</i>

27
00:00:48,100 --> 00:00:50,067
<i>Maybe Andrew is
the one hiding her.</i>

28
00:00:50,633 --> 00:00:51,567
<i> Someone's here.</i>

29
00:00:51,700 --> 00:00:53,400
<i> They might break in.</i>

30
00:00:54,467 --> 00:00:55,833
<i>Joey!
Who are you?</i>

31
00:00:55,967 --> 00:00:57,300
<i> What are you doing there?</i>

32
00:00:57,433 --> 00:00:59,433
<i>It's impossible
that man saw anything.</i>

33
00:00:59,567 --> 00:01:01,200
<i>Are you sure
you didn't see anything?</i>

34
00:01:01,333 --> 00:01:02,533
<i>There's really no one there,
Boss.</i>

35
00:01:02,667 --> 00:01:04,367
<i>Explain everything
to me in detail.</i>

36
00:01:04,500 --> 00:01:06,533
<i>- All right.
- Well, then let's start.</i>

37
00:01:06,667 --> 00:01:07,767
<i> My contact said,</i>

38
00:01:07,933 --> 00:01:10,267
<i>that Golda has already
given a statement.</i>

39
00:01:10,400 --> 00:01:12,300
<i>We have to make sure her
testimony</i>

40
00:01:12,433 --> 00:01:13,633
<i> doesn't see the light of day.</i>

41
00:01:13,767 --> 00:01:15,600
<i> Matias, you know the drill.</i>

42
00:01:34,900 --> 00:01:36,967
I don't have any relationship
with your husband.

43
00:01:39,233 --> 00:01:40,400
That's the truth.

44
00:01:42,733 --> 00:01:45,833
Because of you, my family was
almost destroyed.

45
00:01:46,400 --> 00:01:47,800
I know.

46
00:01:48,533 --> 00:01:52,600
But I really was just
your husband's informant.

47
00:01:53,967 --> 00:01:56,133
Fine, I'll admit it.

48
00:01:56,267 --> 00:01:57,567
I did have a crush on him,

49
00:01:57,700 --> 00:01:58,933
but that's all it was.

50
00:01:59,900 --> 00:02:01,833
He never entertained it.

51
00:02:04,267 --> 00:02:06,133
Your husband is a gentleman.

52
00:02:06,267 --> 00:02:07,933
He's loyal to you.

53
00:02:09,000 --> 00:02:10,600
So I hope...

54
00:02:11,133 --> 00:02:12,500
I hope you can forgive me.

55
00:02:23,467 --> 00:02:25,000
All right.

56
00:02:25,900 --> 00:02:27,967
I forgive you.

57
00:02:28,100 --> 00:02:29,767
Because if you say
anything else,

58
00:02:29,900 --> 00:02:31,800
I might lose
my patience with you.

59
00:02:34,633 --> 00:02:36,400
Sorry again.

60
00:02:37,000 --> 00:02:39,767
I never really wanted
to destroy your family.

61
00:02:39,900 --> 00:02:42,400
I was just scared for my life.

62
00:02:44,333 --> 00:02:46,867
Since Mom already forgave you,

63
00:02:47,900 --> 00:02:49,667
I'm okay with you too.

64
00:02:50,733 --> 00:02:52,467
Thank you, Joey.

65
00:02:53,200 --> 00:02:54,267
I hope...

66
00:02:54,400 --> 00:02:57,167
I hope what I say in court
will really help.

67
00:02:58,000 --> 00:03:00,433
I hope Miguel's name will
finally be cleared...

68
00:03:01,267 --> 00:03:03,433
because he's a good man

69
00:03:04,133 --> 00:03:06,633
and he deserves to be free.

70
00:03:20,200 --> 00:03:21,433
Dad...

71
00:03:24,300 --> 00:03:25,433
Clarissa...

72
00:03:56,500 --> 00:03:59,067
Sorry for doubting you.

73
00:04:00,667 --> 00:04:03,933
Sorry for not believing
your explanations.

74
00:04:05,167 --> 00:04:06,900
You're my husband.

75
00:04:07,033 --> 00:04:09,333
I should have believed you.

76
00:04:10,067 --> 00:04:13,233
Clarissa, I also have my faults.

77
00:04:14,833 --> 00:04:16,833
I've failed you in many ways.

78
00:04:17,967 --> 00:04:20,000
I'm always at work,

79
00:04:20,133 --> 00:04:23,033
so I understand why you started
to doubt me.

80
00:04:27,100 --> 00:04:29,133
From now on, I promise...

81
00:04:30,733 --> 00:04:32,867
I won't doubt you anymore.

82
00:04:33,000 --> 00:04:34,667
You're the one I will believe.

83
00:04:35,333 --> 00:04:38,500
I won't listen to what
other people say anymore.

84
00:04:39,600 --> 00:04:44,533
You and Joey are the only ones
I will believe.

85
00:04:51,467 --> 00:04:53,200
Does this mean

86
00:04:53,333 --> 00:04:54,733
our family is okay again?

87
00:04:54,867 --> 00:04:56,667
Are we whole again?

88
00:04:56,800 --> 00:04:58,300
Joey...

89
00:04:58,833 --> 00:05:00,600
Our family was never broken.

90
00:05:01,767 --> 00:05:03,300
Yes, we were separated

91
00:05:03,433 --> 00:05:07,000
because of the situation
I'm facing now...

92
00:05:08,400 --> 00:05:10,367
but here in my heart,

93
00:05:11,833 --> 00:05:14,067
our family has
always been whole.

94
00:05:16,667 --> 00:05:18,200
Clarissa...

95
00:05:26,200 --> 00:05:27,867
Joey...

96
00:05:29,967 --> 00:05:31,767
I love you so much, Joey.

97
00:05:34,167 --> 00:05:35,767
Clarissa...

98
00:05:36,533 --> 00:05:38,633
I love you very much.

99
00:05:40,467 --> 00:05:42,900
We love you very much too, Dad.

100
00:05:48,533 --> 00:05:50,833
I love you very much too.

101
00:06:04,833 --> 00:06:07,200
Why do you look like that?

102
00:06:07,367 --> 00:06:08,333
Problem?

103
00:06:09,700 --> 00:06:12,400
I'm just having a hard time
accessing the phone

104
00:06:12,533 --> 00:06:15,133
I got from Theresa's date.

105
00:06:15,267 --> 00:06:16,033
Is that all?

106
00:06:16,167 --> 00:06:17,967
I'll check it.

107
00:06:21,233 --> 00:06:22,467
What can you do?

108
00:06:22,867 --> 00:06:24,533
How can you help me?

109
00:06:25,633 --> 00:06:28,833
Fine, I'm already helping you
and you're still being grumpy.

110
00:06:28,967 --> 00:06:31,367
Theresa really got on your
nerves, didn't she?

111
00:06:31,500 --> 00:06:32,967
What?

112
00:06:33,500 --> 00:06:35,800
I'm not grumpy.

113
00:06:38,133 --> 00:06:39,767
Joey is texting.

114
00:06:40,533 --> 00:06:42,167
I got it too.

115
00:06:42,867 --> 00:06:44,167
- Emergency?
- Emergency?

116
00:06:44,833 --> 00:06:47,367
We need volunteers
for the games.

117
00:06:47,500 --> 00:06:50,100
Mom said, this
foundation day event

118
00:06:50,233 --> 00:06:52,200
is held every year
by Ms. Yvette.

119
00:06:52,333 --> 00:06:54,900
Games? What games?

120
00:06:55,033 --> 00:06:56,433
I don't know yet.

121
00:06:56,567 --> 00:06:57,933
Is there a prize?

122
00:06:58,067 --> 00:06:59,533
You're already asking
about prizes?

123
00:06:59,667 --> 00:07:00,700
Well, I don't know.

124
00:07:00,833 --> 00:07:02,933
But even if there isn't a prize,

125
00:07:03,067 --> 00:07:05,133
it's supposed to be fun.

126
00:07:05,267 --> 00:07:06,933
Come on, join.

127
00:07:07,067 --> 00:07:09,567
I'm doing this for Mom.

128
00:07:09,700 --> 00:07:10,833
She's finally happy

129
00:07:10,967 --> 00:07:13,233
because things are clear
between her and Golda,

130
00:07:13,367 --> 00:07:15,433
and everything is okay
between her and Dad.

131
00:07:15,600 --> 00:07:17,600
That's why I agreed too.

132
00:07:17,733 --> 00:07:19,300
And we can think of this

133
00:07:19,433 --> 00:07:21,000
as a break or a vacation

134
00:07:21,133 --> 00:07:22,700
from all our missions.

135
00:07:22,833 --> 00:07:24,300
So, are you game?

136
00:07:24,900 --> 00:07:25,967
I'm in!

137
00:07:26,100 --> 00:07:28,200
- There!
- Oh, come on, It'll be fun!

138
00:07:28,333 --> 00:07:31,200
Come on, let's go!
Let's go, let's go, let's go!

139
00:07:31,333 --> 00:07:33,567
Come on, Jin Ho.
Please join us.

140
00:07:33,700 --> 00:07:36,100
I know you're busy with Theresa.

141
00:07:36,233 --> 00:07:37,433
If I could help you,

142
00:07:37,567 --> 00:07:39,700
I would have done it already.

143
00:07:39,833 --> 00:07:41,167
You'd do that for me?

144
00:07:41,300 --> 00:07:42,667
Of course!

145
00:07:42,800 --> 00:07:44,733
You're my friend, right?

146
00:07:44,867 --> 00:07:47,500
And friends should have fun.
So let's go.

147
00:07:48,400 --> 00:07:49,100
What do you say? Game?

148
00:07:49,233 --> 00:07:51,067
All right, let's go.

149
00:07:51,200 --> 00:07:52,233
- Okay, fine.
- Okay, let's go, let's go!

150
00:07:52,367 --> 00:07:54,200
- Let's go, let's go!
- Let's go.

151
00:07:54,333 --> 00:07:55,600
Oh, go.

152
00:07:57,700 --> 00:08:00,333
Let's go faster!
Come on, hurry!

153
00:08:01,300 --> 00:08:02,733
Let's go!

154
00:08:02,867 --> 00:08:05,100
- Let's go! Let's go!
- Walk faster!

155
00:08:05,233 --> 00:08:07,100
- There.
- Register, register.

156
00:08:07,233 --> 00:08:08,567
- Do you have an extra shirt?
- Right...

157
00:08:08,700 --> 00:08:10,233
that's what I was thinking too.

158
00:08:10,367 --> 00:08:12,167
Let's find one later.

159
00:08:12,300 --> 00:08:13,900
They probably have extras.

160
00:08:14,033 --> 00:08:16,667
But personally,
I didn't bring any.

161
00:08:16,800 --> 00:08:18,300
So what now?

162
00:08:19,067 --> 00:08:21,467
Hey, why are you here?

163
00:08:21,633 --> 00:08:23,167
Are you a stalker?

164
00:08:23,600 --> 00:08:25,067
Stalker?

165
00:08:25,533 --> 00:08:27,633
This is my sister's foundation,

166
00:08:27,767 --> 00:08:30,133
and I join every single year.

167
00:08:30,267 --> 00:08:32,600
Hey, if you're here,
what about Golda?

168
00:08:32,733 --> 00:08:34,333
Aren't you supposed to be
guarding her?

169
00:08:34,467 --> 00:08:35,867
Just relax.

170
00:08:36,400 --> 00:08:38,967
Elai and Kyle
are watching her now.

171
00:08:39,100 --> 00:08:41,633
By the way,
how are your parents?

172
00:08:41,767 --> 00:08:43,400
They finally made up.

173
00:08:43,533 --> 00:08:45,700
But of course, I'm still praying

174
00:08:45,833 --> 00:08:49,067
that all our problems
will truly end.

175
00:08:49,200 --> 00:08:50,800
That's nice.

176
00:08:51,633 --> 00:08:52,800
What about you guys?

177
00:08:52,933 --> 00:08:53,900
What are you guys doing here?

178
00:08:54,033 --> 00:08:55,933
We joined the games.

179
00:08:56,633 --> 00:08:58,167
But what's the prize?

180
00:08:58,300 --> 00:08:59,700
I don't know.

181
00:09:02,067 --> 00:09:05,000
I thought you came here
for charity.

182
00:09:05,133 --> 00:09:06,400
Turns out that's your real
intention.

183
00:09:06,533 --> 00:09:09,433
Of course, that's part of it.

184
00:09:11,500 --> 00:09:12,667
Andrew!

185
00:09:12,800 --> 00:09:13,867
We're about to start.

186
00:09:14,000 --> 00:09:16,100
Oh, are they volunteers?

187
00:09:16,500 --> 00:09:18,100
Yes.

188
00:09:18,600 --> 00:09:20,033
This is Peter.

189
00:09:20,167 --> 00:09:21,800
- This is Jin Ho.
- Hi.

190
00:09:22,433 --> 00:09:24,100
And of course, Joey.

191
00:09:24,233 --> 00:09:27,467
She's Miss Clarissa's daughter.

192
00:09:27,600 --> 00:09:29,267
Thank you for coming.

193
00:09:29,433 --> 00:09:32,600
It's nice to see Andrew
has other friends.

194
00:09:32,733 --> 00:09:34,433
And of course, Joey,

195
00:09:34,567 --> 00:09:37,833
I've heard so many good things
about you from your mom.

196
00:09:37,967 --> 00:09:39,167
Sorry though.

197
00:09:39,300 --> 00:09:40,367
She can't come yet

198
00:09:40,500 --> 00:09:43,433
because some donations just
arrived at headquarters.

199
00:09:43,567 --> 00:09:45,333
She still has to take care
of them.

200
00:09:45,467 --> 00:09:46,333
That's okay.

201
00:09:46,467 --> 00:09:48,367
We'll still do our best.

202
00:09:48,833 --> 00:09:49,667
All right, thank you.

203
00:09:49,800 --> 00:09:51,267
You know, our main objective

204
00:09:51,400 --> 00:09:56,000
is to inspire your partner.

205
00:09:56,133 --> 00:09:57,400
And do your best

206
00:09:57,533 --> 00:10:01,633
because Andrew here is always
the champion in these games,

207
00:10:01,800 --> 00:10:03,867
so whoever gets him
as a partner is lucky.

208
00:10:04,000 --> 00:10:07,000
Wow, so you're really
competitive.

209
00:10:07,767 --> 00:10:09,833
You don't really have
to say that, it's okay.

210
00:10:09,967 --> 00:10:13,333
You already admire
Andrew that much?

211
00:10:13,467 --> 00:10:16,067
I'm sure the challengers
are basic.

212
00:10:16,200 --> 00:10:18,267
Jin Ho and I
haven't even joined yet.

213
00:10:18,400 --> 00:10:19,500
Right, Jin Ho?

214
00:10:19,633 --> 00:10:21,300
- That's true!
- Yes.

215
00:10:21,933 --> 00:10:24,067
You understand Tagalog?

216
00:10:24,200 --> 00:10:25,833
Just a little.

217
00:10:26,167 --> 00:10:27,133
Oh...

218
00:10:27,267 --> 00:10:29,333
His grandma taught him,
so he knows some words,

219
00:10:29,467 --> 00:10:32,933
but he's still not that fluent.

220
00:10:33,067 --> 00:10:35,200
- There.
- That's impressive.

221
00:10:35,367 --> 00:10:37,667
So are we ready?

222
00:10:37,800 --> 00:10:39,500
- Ready! Yes!
- Are you ready? Okay?

223
00:10:39,633 --> 00:10:40,633
Go ahead and register.

224
00:10:40,767 --> 00:10:42,767
- All right.
- Go, Andrew.

225
00:10:43,833 --> 00:10:45,467
Prepare to lose to a Korean.

226
00:10:45,600 --> 00:10:46,433
What?

227
00:10:46,567 --> 00:10:48,467
You know, I'm studying Filipino.

228
00:10:48,600 --> 00:10:51,500
You also study Korean.

229
00:10:56,833 --> 00:11:01,600
Welcome to our foundation's
annual "Palarong Puso!"

230
00:11:07,600 --> 00:11:10,233
This event is not just
for our scholars

231
00:11:10,367 --> 00:11:11,867
but for the kids as well.

232
00:11:12,000 --> 00:11:14,967
You know, it's time for us
to bond

233
00:11:15,100 --> 00:11:18,133
and reward them
for their hard work.

234
00:11:18,267 --> 00:11:19,233
Yehey!

235
00:11:19,367 --> 00:11:21,667
And you guys make me so proud.

236
00:11:21,800 --> 00:11:24,300
And since this is a competition,

237
00:11:24,433 --> 00:11:27,500
every team has to do their best

238
00:11:27,633 --> 00:11:31,233
because we have
so many games today!

239
00:11:33,900 --> 00:11:36,500
And of course,
the final four teams

240
00:11:36,633 --> 00:11:38,567
with the highest points

241
00:11:38,700 --> 00:11:40,533
will face each other at the end

242
00:11:40,700 --> 00:11:43,100
in a tug of war.

243
00:11:43,233 --> 00:11:46,367
So you need to strategize!

244
00:11:49,600 --> 00:11:50,533
Hey, you're so noisy.

245
00:11:50,667 --> 00:11:52,533
You're acting like
you're already the winner.

246
00:11:52,667 --> 00:11:55,867
The team that wins third place
will take home...

247
00:11:56,000 --> 00:11:56,900
How much is that?

248
00:11:57,033 --> 00:11:58,767
3,000 pesos!

249
00:12:00,000 --> 00:12:02,833
Yes, and second place

250
00:12:02,967 --> 00:12:05,267
will take home a whopping

251
00:12:05,400 --> 00:12:08,200
5,000 pesos!

252
00:12:10,333 --> 00:12:12,400
- And of course...
- What?

253
00:12:12,533 --> 00:12:13,533
The champion...

254
00:12:13,667 --> 00:12:16,100
The champion will take home...

255
00:12:16,267 --> 00:12:17,200
How much?

256
00:12:17,333 --> 00:12:19,367
10,000 pesos!

257
00:12:21,867 --> 00:12:23,467
But before that,

258
00:12:23,600 --> 00:12:26,433
before we finish,
just a reminder,

259
00:12:26,567 --> 00:12:28,200
have fun, okay?

260
00:12:28,333 --> 00:12:30,233
So what are we waiting for?

261
00:12:30,367 --> 00:12:33,367
Let the games begin!

262
00:12:35,400 --> 00:12:37,867
Okay, we'll start
with this game.

263
00:12:38,000 --> 00:12:41,433
And partner, let's call it...

264
00:12:41,567 --> 00:12:44,033
- Last Egg Standing!
- Last Egg Standing!

265
00:12:48,400 --> 00:12:50,300
This game is very simple.

266
00:12:50,433 --> 00:12:52,933
When you hear Madam's whistle,

267
00:12:53,067 --> 00:12:56,067
